      "id": "n1",
      "kind": "usage",
      "title": "ชอบ and มาก",
      "text": "ชอบ means \"to like\", and ไม่ชอบ means \"do not like\". Put มาก after a word to say \"a lot\": ชอบมาก.",
      "explains": [
        "th.like-chop",
        "th.degree-mak"
      ],
      "afterScenes": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "n2",
      "kind": "grammar",
      "title": "แต่ means but",
      "text": "แต่ joins two ideas that pull against each other, with no comma and no space: ชอบขนมแต่ไม่ชอบกาแฟ. In Thai the whole sentence is one run of letters.",
      "explains": [
        "th.but-tae"
      ],
      "afterScenes": 1
    }
  ],
